| `secrets.scanner.history_log_opts` | list of strings | `["--all"]` | a non-empty list of `git log` options, none blank or holding whitespace | `scripts/scan_secrets.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `secrets.scanner.history_log_opts` row | Sets which commits the history scan reaches: the scanner runs `git log -p -U0` with these options. Narrowing it hides commits from the scan, so it is a security decision. Options that reach no commit are exit 13 (`NOTHING_JUDGED`), never a clean scan, and an option git refuses is exit 2. An option holding whitespace is refused, because the scanner splits the list on spaces. Absent, the scan writes `[using default] secrets.scanner.history_log_opts = ["--all"]` to stderr. | the staged scan, which judges the index whatever this holds | always |
